  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For real numbers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, let</p><p>Area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p><p>and</p><p>Area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8805;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p><p>Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow/><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to _____.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that area of circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is radius of circle)&nbsp;and area of ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;ab</mi></math>&nbsp;(where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;are length of semi major and semi minor axis)</p><p>Now given area between circle and ellipse&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp; .....(i)</p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;....(ii)</p><p>On subtracting equation (i) - (ii), we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
